Here’s a structured, production-level description of the **AccelRestaurants™ Digital Menu & Growth Platform**, grounded in your current MVP app, the tile types list, and your restaurant-services positioning.

---

## 1. Platform Identity & Vision

**Name (working):** AccelRestaurants™ – Digital Menu & Growth Platform
**Owner:** Accel Analysis, LLC
**Branding:** Visual style, typography, and tone aligned with the main Accel Analysis site (dark-neutral backgrounds, orange highlights, clean typography, “Clarity. Strategy. Execution.”). ([Accel Analysis Business Solutions][1])

**High-level promise:**

> “Turn local data into full tables, stronger tickets, and smarter growth” for restaurants, cafés, and food concepts, unifying **digital menu boards**, **hyper-targeted campaigns**, and **KPI dashboards** into a single platform. ([Accel Analysis][2])

The platform is not just a screen-designer. It is:

1. A **multi-tenant digital signage system** for restaurant menu & promo screens.
2. A **menu & offer strategy tool** that reuses the same items across print, screens, and campaigns. ([Accel Analysis][2])
3. A **campaign & KPI layer** that ties digital boards to hyper-targeted direct mail, radius-based outreach, and restaurant performance dashboards. ([Accel Analysis][2])

---

## 2. Current MVP Baseline (What Already Exists)

Based on the attached React app: 

* **Frontend only**, single-page React app.
* Three main views (stateful in `RestaurantSignageApp`):

  * **Dashboard**:

    * Manages **Locations**.
    * Each location has multiple **Screens** positioned on a layout canvas (drag to x,y).
    * Each Screen references a set of **Slides** (by ID) and a rotation duration.
    * “Slide Library” on the left, drag slides onto the location layout to create screens.
  * **Slide Editor**:

    * Canvas (800×450) representing one slide.
    * Left: palette of `TILE_TYPES` icons.
    * Center: drag-and-drop tile elements, each with x,y,width,height,zIndex.
    * Right: layout & type-specific property panel for the selected tile.
  * **Display**:

    * Fullscreen “player” for a selected screen.
    * Cycles through that screen’s slides with a global rotation interval.
* **Persistence**:

  * Local only (React state), with **Import/Export JSON** buttons.

This will become the **core “Screens & Slides” module** of the production platform.

---

## 3. Canonical Tile System

### 3.1 Base Tile Types (Global “Type Registry”)

The platform’s **canonical tile types** come from `types list.txt` (the “type registry”). 

Each row is a base **TileType** with:

* `key` (e.g., `text`, `image`, `video`, `qrcode`).
* Human label & description.
* Base property schema (content, color, etc.).
* Notes about behavior (e.g., “uses wttr.in,” “uses <model-viewer>,” etc.).

Examples (abbreviated):

* `text` – multi-line static text.
* `image` / `gif` / `video` / `youtube` / `vimeo` – media tiles for media URLs.
* `shape` / `gradient` – backgrounds/containers.
* `qrcode` – QR generator tile.
* `scene` – background slideshow.
* `weather`, `weather_detailed`, `weather_icon`, `emojiWeather` – different weather representations.
* `bar`, `pie`, `table` – simple data visualizations.
* `sheetcell` – value pulled from Google Sheets cell.
* `rss`, `marquee`, `quote` – text feeds & motion.
* `status`, `progress` – indicator tiles.
* `html`, `iframe` – controlled HTML and embed tiles.
* `openai` – AI-generated text tile (requires API key).
* Others like `3dmodel`, `lottie`, `map`, `menu`, `timer`, etc.

**Production rule:**

* The **only “base” tile types** are those in this registry.
* Restaurant-specific cards (e.g., “Menu Item Card”, “Daily Deal”) are **Tile Templates** (see below), not new base types.

The current MVP’s expanded `TILE_TYPES` list (menuItem, specialBanner, wifiDetails, placeholder types, etc.) will be migrated and collapsed into:

* **Base types**: mapped to registry (`text`, `image`, `video`, `shape`, `clock`, `weather`, `qrcode`, `html`, `iframe`, etc.).
* **Template tiles**: saved presets built on those base types (e.g., “Dessert Highlight”, “WiFi Details”, “Daily Deal Banner”). 

### 3.2 Tile Templates (Restaurant & User Presets)

**Goal:** Allow users to save styling + behavior of any base tile as a **Template** they can reuse.

**Entity: `TileTemplate`**

* `id`
* `organizationId` (restaurant account)
* `createdByUserId`
* `tileTypeKey` (e.g., `text`, `image`, `menu`)
* `name` (e.g., “Burger Price Label – White Bold 36px”)
* `tags` (e.g., `["price", "lunch", "hero-item"]`)
* `defaultProps` (JSON of tile properties; exactly matches base tile prop schema)
* `thumbnailUrl` (optional screenshot generated server-side for palette)

**Usage:**

* Palette in the Slide Editor gains **two tabs**:

  * **Base Tiles** (from type registry).
  * **My Templates** (user-created, account-specific).
* Dragging a template onto the canvas creates a **TileInstance** pre-populated with its `defaultProps`.

**Create / Edit Flow:**

1. User adds a base tile on a slide and customizes fonts, colors, border radius, content bindings, etc.
2. User clicks **“Save as Template”**:

   * Names template.
   * Assigns tags (e.g., “Combo Offer”, “Happy Hour Banner”).
3. Template appears in **My Templates** for this organization.
4. Editing an existing template:

   * User can change default props.
   * Default behavior: **changes affect future placements only**.
   * Optional advanced behavior (Phase 2): “Update linked instances” to propagate style changes to tiles that are explicitly linked.

